## Getting started

### 1. Requirements
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) LTS (v18 or newer)
- A free Gemini API key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey

### 2. Clone
```bash
git clone https://github.com/bhupendrasinghbs/Exam-Preap-AI.git
cd Exam-Preap-AI
```

### 3. Backend (port 5000)
```bash
cd backend
cp .env.example .env      # on Windows: copy .env.example .env
npm install
npm run dev
```

Edit `backend/.env`:
```dotenv
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
PORT=5000
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
```
Model names change often. If you get a model "not found" error, check the current names at https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models and update `GEMINI_MODEL`. The fallback model is used automatically if the main one is overloaded.

### 4. Frontend (port 5173)
Open a second terminal:
```bash
cd frontend
cp .env.example .env
npm install
npm run dev
```
Open http://localhost:5173.

> The frontend needs **Tailwind CSS v3**. If you see a PostCSS/Tailwind error, run `npm install -D tailwindcss@3 postcss autoprefixer`.

